# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-plugin-epure — the EPURE plug-in (BricsCAD and AutoCAD launched under the EPURE profile)
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: feature
#+DEPENDS: alfe-plugin-hooks
#+BRANCH: master

* Context

First plug-in of =alfe-plugin-model=. What the legacy tools did
(=~/works/sncf-reseau/scripts/autocad-epure=, =bricscad-epure=, and the old
=autolisp-script/autolisp-deprecated= wrapper, functions
=windows_epure_control_script=, =run_windows_bricscad=,
=run_windows_autocad=, and the VBS bridge):

- =cd "<CAD install dir>\UserDataCache"= then
  =acad.exe /p Epure /b "%APPDATA%\sncf\epure\epure 2022\control_path_epure_2022.scr"=
  (AutoCAD) or
  =bricscad.exe /p Epure /b "%APPDATA%\sncf\epure\epure 2022_b\control_path_epure_2022.scr"=
  (BricsCAD): the profile is =Epure= and EPURE is started by *running its
  control script*.
- The wrapper's =run.scr= began with =._SCRIPT= + that script's path, then
  =(load run-common.lsp)=. BricsCAD was forced to batch (COM off);
  AutoCAD under COM activated the profile with
  =app.Preferences.Profiles.ActiveProfile= and sent =._SCRIPT= before the
  load; =--epure= with accoreconsole was refused (no profile support).
- Windows only; ignored elsewhere.

* Proposal

Plug-in =epure= (=autolisp-front-end/plugins/epure/epure.lisp=), applies to
=:bricscad= and =:autocad= on Windows.

- Options: =--epure= (activation), =--epure-profile NAME= (default =Epure=),
  =--epure-script FILE= (default: the =%APPDATA%= path above, per CAD).
  Env: =$AUTOLISP_EPURE=, =$AUTOLISP_EPURE_PROFILE=, =$AUTOLISP_EPURE_SCRIPT=.
- =:cli-parsed=: not Windows or backend clautolisp → deactivate quietly
  (verbose log; the documented "silently ignored"). AutoCAD: default the
  mode to =automation= (COM); an explicit =--mode batch= (accoreconsole)
  is a usage error. BricsCAD: default =batch=; =--mode automation= is
  honoured.
- =:backend-selected=: the control script must exist, else
  =backend-bootstrap-error= naming the path searched (exit 4).
- =:launch-argv= (BricsCAD batch): drop =/Automation= (EPURE is a full-GUI
  application), replace any =/p PROFILE= pair by =/p Epure=.
- =:launch-options=: working directory =<exe dir>\UserDataCache= when it
  exists.
- =:launcher-lines= (SCR): =._SCRIPT= then the control script's path, before
  the =(load run-common.lsp)=. (VBS): profile activation after the
  application exists, =._SCRIPT= via =SendCommand= before the load.
- =run-common.lsp= is not touched.

* Not verifiable here

No Windows, no EPURE, no CAD: everything is asserted with the mock CAD,
=--print-command= and =*host-os-override*= = =:windows=. Whether a
=._SCRIPT= nested in a =/b= script returns control to the outer script,
and whether the GUI stays usable, are the two questions the real-CAD run
(=alfe-plugin-epure-windows-validation=) answers.

* Acceptance criteria

- =--print-command --bricscad --epure= (Windows override) prints
  =bricscad.exe … /p Epure /b …\run.scr= without =/Automation=, and the
  staged =run.scr= chains the control script before the load.
- =--autocad --epure= selects automation; =--autocad --mode batch --epure=
  is refused; the staged VBS carries the profile and script lines.
- Off Windows, and under =--clautolisp=, =--epure= changes nothing.
